findings:
  - id: AOOSR-R4-IR-B01
    severity: blocker
    title: Delayed scanner self-replacement escapes the claimed module cleanup closure
    contract_surface:
      - control-plane/registry/drafts/2026-07-25-agents-os-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r4-amendment-v0.1.md
      - control-plane/registry/run-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r4.py
    evidence: >-
      _load_verified_scanner removes its mapping only in the finally block around
      exec and then returns. A matching-digest synthetic scanner started a thread
      that waited on a deterministic Event. The loader returned successfully and
      had no mapping at that instant. After the Event was set, the scanner thread
      reinstalled sys.modules[VERIFIED_SCANNER_MODULE_NAME]. The mapping was
      present, so this is a self-replacing scanner accepted by the loader rather
      than a rejected cleanup violation.
    impact: >-
      R4 does not establish its required invariant that a self-replacing scanner
      fails closed and leaves no mapping. The module lifecycle can therefore be
      altered after the loader's terminal cleanup check.
    required_R5_scope:
      - close_post_return_or_asynchronous_self_replacement_and_residual_mapping
      - retain_digest_before_execution_collision_preservation_and_fixed_scanner_boundary
      - add_the_deterministic_delayed_Event_self_replacement_as_a_fixed_negative_probe
      - keep_R1_to_R4_fixed_bytes_immutable_and_do_not_run_actual_or_Host_paths

